<p>Iran said it was reviewing a new U.S. proposal to end the war, while President Trump said Washington and Tehran had held “very good talks” and that a deal was “very possible”. Reuters, carried by Al-Monitor, reported that sources described the proposal as a plan that would formally end the conflict while leaving unresolved Washington’s demands that Iran suspend its nuclear program and reopen the Strait of Hormuz. Trump also threatened resumed U.S. attacks if Iran rejected a deal; CBS reported he threatened a “higher level” of strikes, and several accounts said he warned bombing would resume at a higher level and intensity if negotiations failed. Iranian officials disputed accounts of an imminent agreement, with Foreign Ministry spokesman Esmaeil Baqaei saying the U.S. proposal remained under review and reports cited by Haaretz and Aaj TV saying parliament speaker Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf pushed back against claims of rapid progress. The talks focus on nuclear limits and shipping access through the Strait of Hormuz, where wartime restrictions have disrupted commercial transit. PBS and Business Times reported that the draft under discussion was preliminary and that follow-on negotiations were expected if both sides accepted it.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ZBs2TtJYHJXS5tlGQgQHoRjkg-3LEymR8YGcc_i_JymzYCNNebSPPWxxldmhW2ZoMRGJQMqBLydQFJEYsJ4kt0vroZORrniUKSnT3HH072fTm1XBwsWKRUWHlyXxV5RAkN83FtQ3hLqbQYOhUx1Kp-O-F5NYxCzDnIYimc6PNddJwhpMJrKsRfBFO0MtPP9InGd1cWg8' alt='A woman walks near a Tehran billboard depicting the Strait of Hormuz with a Persian caption reading &quot;Forever in Iran&#x27;s Hand&quot; on May 6, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Uranium stockpile: President Trump said the United States would receive enriched uranium from Iran; Reuters reported Iran had not handed over more than 900 pounds, or 408 kg, of highly enriched uranium.</li><li>Hormuz operation: President Trump halted a short-lived U.S. military operation to reopen the Strait of Hormuz while seeking a deal, according to AFP-based reports carried by Channels Television and Business Recorder.</li><li>Iranian objections: Channels Television and Business Recorder said Iran’s chief negotiator warned Washington was seeking to force the Islamic republic’s “surrender”.</li><li>Sanctions component: Nation reported that sanctions relief and a Lebanon ceasefire were among the items included in a preliminary package alongside nuclear and Hormuz provisions.</li></ul><blockquote>We’ve had very good talks over the last 24 hours, and it’s very possible that we’ll make a deal - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: He said Washington would see whether Iran could make a deal “satisfactory to us.” (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/trump-says-iran-wants-make-deal'>Reuters via Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Iranian critics: Iranian officials criticized the U.S. proposal; Aaj TV said lawmaker Ebrahim Rezaei called it “more of an American wish list than a reality,” while Business Recorder reported a negotiator warning against forced “surrender.” (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330458474/trump-optimistic-on-iran-deal-says-war-could-be-over-quickly'>Aaj TV</a>, <a href='https://www.brecorder.com/news/40419982/trump-says-iran-deal-very-possible'>Business Recorder</a>)</li><li>Pakistan: Pakistan said it was mediating and working to turn the ceasefire into a permanent end to the war. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cj0pq2q8221o'>BBC</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/trump-sees-swift-end-war-iran-reviews-us-peace-proposal'>Trump sees swift end to war as Iran reviews US peace proposal</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/iran-peace-proposal-trump-ceasefire-hormuz/33751441.html'>Tehran Reviews Latest US Proposal Amid Trump Optimism -- And Threats</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show